{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced","id":1131067,"title":"Kith and Kin book announced.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-18T19:18:32-07:00","id":1131067,"title":"Kith and Kin book announced.","content":"From the Panel, Changeling is getting a book on Kiths after the Hedge called Kith and Kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:19:46-07:00","id":1131068,"title":"","content":"Like Seanan Mcguire Stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:49:08-07:00","id":1131088,"title":"","content":"I must've not heard this when I listened. Was anything more said? A book of Kiths doesn't seem like the dev's style.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nope, there it is. How odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-18-2017, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:51:27-07:00","id":1131090,"title":"","content":"This sounds good. I mean.. consider this. MA lot of us got attached to David's version of Seeming, and feel a little lost right now, especially if we converted groups to 1.5. If there is going to be a book discussing HOW a seeming and kith can come about, including reconstructions, reconstructions, and entirely weird outliers, that patches that wound up nicely. I'd expect it won't just be lists of new Kitts, but also where we hear about other things like Grimm, the Wyrd-chosen (if they still exist), and the idea of Loyalists being a seeming or unique seemings somehow (an idea in was so proud I almost got into the books, but hope will still come up). plus more kith and ''lost seemings'' would be awesome as it is (was there a pixie seeming between Victorian England and the day the modern Disney fairies died, where most fae were tiny winged miscreants?).. I like that concept. There are definitely certain writers i'd hope get involved, one whose arcane name shant be mentioned, but.. I think this is the place where we can fix the bridges burned, so to speak. Especially if Kith and kin covers the racial identity stuff that winter masques covered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":".  autocorrect once again 08-18-2017, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T20:50:07-07:00","id":1131108,"title":"","content":"whatever, i'll take it. i was hoping that we would get a &quot;rites of spring&quot; type of book, with more fairy magic and subsystems and merits. but i guess a kith book is cool. like, i'm not super into character creation as a mini-game so all that front end option stuff sorta leaves me a cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T22:07:50-07:00","id":1131123,"title":"","content":"Remember Firefly, the 2e books have a new trend compared to 1e. In 1e, there was an idea that supplements were all... independent. that is, you don't have to buy more than one if you don't want to. The supplements introduced awesome mechanics, but the gameline as a whole had to treat those rules as optional. Great ideas in games had to either be carefully retreaded (in changeling, see dual kith and true fae rules) or ignored. While I agree with the idea as a whole, keeping supplements self contained, it does suck when awesome new ideas come from a supplement and thus aren't entirely canon.<br /> <br /> 2e has been great about that so far. Many of the best optional rules from 1e are specifically built into the corebook now, and that's according to at least the vampire, mage, promethean, and changeling developers. You can look at the most epic supplement borne merits of any race, and they're now in the core. They learned what ideas were really so integral to the story of a gameline that those options were moved to the codebook, just in case the producers in whitewolf stick with the ''no supplement should need to refer to another for rules'' thing. Having gotten every 2e core so far, every single one had the equivalent of Rites of Spring built in. Changeling included--notice that Dave's spoilers of changeling merits included a lot of the flavor merits from rites of spring, much like how vamps, weres, mages, and prometheans got a lot of their best supplement born merits in the core, and I'd bet Rose has added more flavors.<br /> <br /> Based on that, and knowing the writers and developers, I would assume that anything from Rites of Spring, Dancers in the Dusk, Equinox Road... anything that really is something to either keep or vastly change, we will either see it said in the corebook or, like belial's brood and the pure, they're still brewing it for later. They'll include much more that we need this time, like the other cores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":".  arguing with autocorrect 08-19-2017, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:33:27-07:00","id":1131205,"title":"","content":"&quot;Kith and Kin&quot;...could also throw a few more friendly fae things in there. Other things that use kith at least. Something to keep in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","ava