"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:12:50-07:00","id":1131437,"title":"","content":"I'm betting there's be some Fae-Touched and children of Changelings in the Kin part of Kith and Kin too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:40:36-07:00","id":1131443,"title":"","content":"I am so excited to hear that this book is in the works. I love kiths (both reading and writing them), so even if it was just a book of kiths, I'd be delighted. I doubt that it will be so limited, though. I have high hopes that this will give us the children of Fae beings as well, and perhaps some other strange things as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:18:22-07:00","id":1131494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131384#post1131384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">same here!</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps playable Fetches (if they aren't playable from core), would be a good stretch Goal to add to Kith and Kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:19:31-07:00","id":1131495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131437#post1131437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm betting there's be some Fae-Touched and children of Changelings in the Kin part of Kith and Kin too</div> </div> </div> </div> FaeTouched are in the core, but I could see offspring of the FAE explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:20:33-07:00","id":1131496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131443#post1131443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so excited to hear that this book is in the works. I love kiths (both reading and writing them), so even if it was just a book of kiths, I'd be delighted. I doubt that it will be so limited, though. I have high hopes that this will give us the children of Fae beings as well, and perhaps some other strange things as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well it will also have, Kith powers and rules for making your own Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T17:25:12-07:00","id":1131522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131496#post1131496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and rules for making your own Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the CtL2e core was going to have those rules by default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:53:45-07:00","id":1131595,"title":"","content":"I would also love to see non-human changelings. That is hobgoblins and even Huntsmen that became half-human in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:54:53-07:00","id":1131596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131495#post1131495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FaeTouched are in the core, but I could see offspring of the FAE explored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be cool to show not only the offspring between Changelings and humans, but also families that have a strong connection to the fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:55:54-07:00","id":1131687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131522#post1131522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the CtL2e core was going to have those rules by default?</div> </div> </div> </div> I assume they meant expanded, more detailed rules for making Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:56:37-07:00","id":1131712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131687#post1131687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume they meant expanded, more detailed rules for making Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe <i>advises</i> on creating Kiths will be in supplement? Like 'good ideas are X, Y, Z' ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T13:25:39-07:00","id":1131860,"title":"","content":"I hope that Kin and Kith book has a True Love type merit. I know that a True Love merit already exists in the Chronicles of Darkness Universe, but believe it is specific to Mages.<br /> <br /> Here is my rough draft for a Changeling True Love Merit. Suggestions would be much appreciated<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b><i>True Love( 1 to 4 dots)</i></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Prerequisite:</i></b> Resolve 3, Composure 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Effects: </i></b>Being entities incapable or true emotions, sometimes the greatest weapons a changeling has against one of True Fae are their feelings and one of our greatest emotions is love. Love gives us the power to overcome obstacles, conquer our fears, and even override our failings. It was the changelings love for their families that allowed them to overcome the seductions of their Keepers and Arcadia. This doesn\u2019t have to be love between spouses or lovers, but can be a parents love for their child, the bond between siblings, or a friendship stronger than blood.</span></span></span><br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b><i>Souls Cry:</i></b> The Changeling can sense when their loved one is in danger and have a clear idea of where they are.</li> <li><b><i>I Know You:</i></b> The changeling can see through all disguises of their loved one and even when their loved one is transformed to hide them from the changeling.</li> <li><b><i>A Hero Lies in You: </i></b>The changeling gets +2 in all resolve and heroic actions dealing with rescuing or protecting their loved one.</li> <li><b><i>Loves True Kiss:</i></b> By kissing their loved one on the lips or cheek, they can release them from the hold of any enchantment.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T16:08:28-07:00","id":1131932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131712#post1131712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe <i>advises</i> on creating Kiths will be in supplement? Like 'good ideas are X, Y, Z' ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T17:47:56-07:00","id":1131963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131596#post1131596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be cool to show not only the offspring between Changelings and humans, but also families that have a strong connection to the fae.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For example, according to tradition the banshee can only cry for five major Irish families: the O\u2019Grady\u2019s, the O\u2019Neills, the O\u2019Longs, the McCnaimhins, the O\u2019Briens, the O\u2019 Conchobhairs, and the Caomhanachs. Intermarriage has since extended this select list. The idea I have is that the Banshee kith was originally created from members of these families.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:52:31-07:00","id":1132009,"title":"","content":"Going off of the trend with the Pack, and Secrets of the Covenants, for 2E, it could be possible that Kith &amp; Kin is a in-game look at changelings by way of fluff. Especially if Kin = Seeming. Maybe with an appendix filled with crunch-ups of the flavor? I dunno, maybe that's just wishful thinking on my end, haha. I'm a fan of the clanbook-esque supplements, and Changeling would certainly be an interesting perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14044-kingbuji","name":"kingbuji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14044_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:26:11-07:00","id":1132054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingbuji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1132009#post1132009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going off of the trend with the Pack, and Secrets of the Covenants, for 2E, it could be possible that Kith &amp; Kin is a in-game look at changelings by way of fluff. Especially if Kin = Seeming. Maybe with an appendix filled with crunch-ups of the flavor? I dunno, maybe that's just wishful thinking on my end, haha. I'm a fan of the clanbook-esque supplements, and Changeling would certainly be an interesting perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pack doesn't feel like a fluff book to me, and is in a different format than Secrets of the Covenants. Those are a very different style of supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T00:09:03-07:00","id":1132110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1132054#post1132054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Pack doesn't feel like a fluff book to me, and is in a different format than Secrets of the Covenants. Those are a very different style of supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haha, honestly, I've only just started reading the Pack, so I think I misspoke. Been rereading the VtR clanbooks back-to-back, so I think my brain is stuck in that kind of formatting. My mistake!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14044-kingbuji","name":"kingbuji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14044_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T01:37:12-07:00","id":1132120,"title":"","content":"I really hope we don't end up with clan book style book for Changeling, only way it would make sense is for Seasonal Courts and so many parts of the world wont have Seasonal Court systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:10:55-07:00","id":1132343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1131067-kith-and-kin-book-announced?p=1131090#post1131090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds good. I mean.. consider this. MA lot of us got attached to David's version of Seeming, and feel a little lost right now, especially if we converted groups to 1.5. If there is going to be a book discussing HOW a seeming and kith can come about, including reconstructions, reconstructions, and entirely weird outliers, that patches that wound up nicely. I'd expect it won't just be lists of new Kitts, but also where we hear about other things like Grimm, the Wyrd-chosen (if they still exist), and the idea of Loyalists being a seeming or unique seemings somehow (an idea in was so proud I almost got into the books, but hope will still come up). plus more kith and ''lost seemings'' would be awesome as it is (was there a pixie seeming between Victorian England and the day the modern Disney fairies died, where most fae were tiny winged miscreants?).. I like that concept. There are definitely certain writers i'd hope get involved, one whose arcane name shant be mentioned, but.. I think this is the place where we can fix the bridges burned, so to speak. Especially if Kith and kin covers the racial identity stuff that winter masques covered?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I would like to see is the idea of a fae-touched gaining a kith through their own efforts rather than the will/power of a Gentry/True Fae. That is, A fae-touched enters Arcadia to rescue a family member or friend and through their actions and desires gains a kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}